# Round-3 housekeeping. Proving a fix in apps/web/scripts/assert-no-inlined-secrets.mjs
# sometimes needs a real Next.js build with a temporary component reading an env var — always
# deleted immediately after each proof, but this backstops that manual cleanup in case a step
# is interrupted mid-round, so a probe file can never be swept into a commit by an unrelated
# `git add`.
_probe-*
_leak-test-*
# Route-handler probes can't use a leading underscore — Next.js treats a leading-underscore
# folder as a private, non-routed folder, which would make the probe route unreachable and
# defeat the point of proving it. This pattern covers that case instead.
app/probe-*
